<<~ ahu #/markdown-otakiage-20261031>>

!! Evergreen routing after the operator-approved Markdown fire

The living human entry points are now `tools/projection-loom/README.md` and `tools/projection-loom/docs/HANDOFF.md`. The old Projection Loom design, research, roadmap, kanban, guidebook, example and temporary ashes Markdown paths were retired from the working tree on PR #84 by explicit operator direction. Their byte-exact prior state is recoverable with `git show 864dc19e89a913ac82862b842202bfce0c68e16b:<path>` (and older complete living fronts at `7c644e670390ab51aaa39e9216bb833eb32e6762`). Git is the ashes carrier. Earlier sections naming retired `.md` paths are historical source references, not current runnable links; never infer those files still exist in the working tree.

A dedicated archive ref `archive/pr84-before-lares-ashes-retirement-20261031` preserves the full former carrier bytes even after PR squash. Root-bag Lares carriers remain the semantic owners; no second authority or evolution controller is created. The mutation-first versus reconstruction-first dispute remains kept testimony, not proof of a native-admitted descendant. Source bodies, STEP evidence, lineages and original research attributions survive this documentation retirement. Exact-head CI, repository-wide consumer reconciliation and code-path acceptance remain independent duties.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/yin-living>>

!! YIN · Native topology and fixed-camera operator review

PR #84 remains open, working `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--projection-loom`. The complete boot lives on `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5` under `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot.mem`. Read it and the actual PR head/Actions; predecessor green results never transfer.

This campaign grows full-authorized two/three-hop spatial circulation under original `connect/shelter/ascend/bear` obligations. The `place_three_hop` constructor builds an operator-named x-y-x or y-x-y three-leg chain with two new original-source-preserving native corner foundations. The equal-budget `place_topology_study` compares those against the prior two-hop alternatives under the same site. An original foundation obstructing a proposed waypoint yields typed `construction-refused` testimony in the study; other alternatives continue to their own STEP auditions, and refused arms consume no fabricated native budget. Each completed route carries independent observed hops, axes, original goal consequences and reimported STEP evidence.

The new `place_topology_gallery` uses the existing frozen CAD gallery cameras and independent native STEP meshes to render six-view sheets for each constructible arm. A read-only HTML board holds all choices and every source-construction refusal without auto-selecting a winner. Native scene identities, camera receipts, image SHA-256, HTML SHA-256 and every source-bound trial remain independently replayable. CLI run/verify routes both topology study and gallery through typed original source. They form an evidence and presentation study, **not a second OODA-HA controller**.

The first published topology head `564eab24fab0c3471fe2e3ed8c68d820446fa0b7` triggered native and repo CI; at inspection its six-view and several native support witnesses were green, while full CAD and generalized integration remained in progress. This new staged gallery head must earn its own exact-head verdict. No artistic winner, automatic operator acceptance, pet-name, Elyncia canon, structural safety certificate, source-camera registration, real Unreal Editor success, PR merge or final o-takiage follows.

Read `tools/projection-loom/README.md`, `tools/projection-loom/docs/HANDOFF.md` and the root-bag Lares research/design/crew carriers for present intent and open limits. Old source paths live only in the Git archives; the operator authorized their retirement.

<<~/ahu>>

